      "nets": ["PWM", "SDA", "SCK"],
      "observed": "Both the ATtiny45 (U2) and ATtiny13 (U3) are present in the component list, and their corresponding I/O pins are directly connected to the same signal nets. In particular, their PB1 pins share PWM, and their PB0 and PB2 pins share SDA and SCK.",
      "expected": "Only one MCU should be populated, or the MCU connections should be isolated so that two devices cannot drive shared signal nets simultaneously. The files show no assembly-exclusion indication for either MCU.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U2\") (value \"ATtiny45-20P\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U3\") (value \"ATtiny13V-10S\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"10\") (name \"PWM\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") ...) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"13\") (name \"SDA\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"5\") ...) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"5\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"12\") (name \"SCK\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"7\") ...) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"7\") ...))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both MCUs are assembled, their shared outputs may contend when they drive different logic levels, disrupting PWM or other signals and potentially stressing the MCU output pins. This may be intended as an either/or package option, but the supplied design files do not mark either device as excluded from assembly.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist connects two separately listed MCUs pin-for-pin on their power and signal nets, including the PWM output. Unless assembly is restricted to one MCU, the shared outputs can contend."
}

